    "title": "❄️⛅ Your Spokane Thursday could see some light snow early, with much warmer, and nice conditions on deck - Jason - NewsBreak",
    "text": "11 hours ago Hello there! A chilly Wednesday is setting up another cold day ahead, with a chance for light snow in the Idaho Panhandle and the Spokane region—then much warmer temperatures arrive soon.\nThursday: Before 11 a.m., a few quick snow showers are possible. Impacts should be minor, and most snow will melt quickly. Around an inch is possible near Sandpoint and Bonners Ferry. By afternoon, scattered showers are likely with lighter winds (5–10 mph). Sunshine returns heading into the weekend.\nA Freeze Warning is in effect for parts of central Washington, including Moses Lake, Ritzville, and Wenatchee, from 2 a.m. to 8 a.m. Thursday. These alerts help agricultural areas protect sensitive crops from damaging freezing temperatures.\n7-day outlook: Beautiful conditions build in late Thursday and into the weekend—lots of sunshine, with 60s returning Saturday and 70s by Monday. After Thursday, it looks mostly dry.\nStay warm!\n-Jason\nCOPYRIGHT 2026 BY KXLY. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. THIS MATERIAL MAY NOT BE PUBLISHED, BROADCAST, REWRITTEN OR REDISTRIBUTED.",
    "summary": "A chilly Wednesday is setting up another cold day ahead, with a chance for light snow in the Idaho Panhandle and the Spokane region—then much warmer temperatures arrive soon. By afternoon, scattered showers are likely with lighter winds (5–10 mph). A Freeze Warning is in effect for parts of central Washington, including Moses Lake, Ritzville, and Wenatchee, from 2 a.m. to 8 a.m. Thursday. These alerts help agricultural areas protect sensitive crops from damaging freezing temperatures. 7-day outlook: Beautiful conditions build in late Thursday and into the weekend—lots of sunshine, with 60s returning Saturday and 70s by Monday.",
